 s-a-2027-perspective\n\nThe Stanford Cancer Institute Breakthroughs in Can
 cer seminar series provides a platform for eminent leaders in oncology to 
 share their insights with the Stanford community. Seminars highlight innov
 ations across basic\, translational\, clinical\, and population cancer sci
 ence. \n\nJoin us Tuesday\, June 8\, 2027\, 4-5 p.m.\, at Gunn Rotunda (E2
 41)\, ChEM-H Building and Neurosciences Building\, or Zoom for a presentat
 ion by Hagop Kantarjian\, MD. Kantarjian is a professor in the Department 
 of Leukemia and holds the Samsung Distinguished Leukemia Chair in Cancer M
 edicine at MD Anderson Cancer Center.\n\nThe event is open to Stanford fac
 ulty\, trainees\, students\, and staff.\n\nRegistration is encouraged.
